# Template for .env.local — copy it and fill in your own values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is git-ignored, so real credentials stay on your machine.
# The server reads these at startup. Values already exported in your shell take
# precedence over the file; anything missing falls back to the local
# db/docker-compose.yml database, so you can run with no .env.local at all.
#
# These are the libpq standard variable names, so the same file also works for
# psql, the Prisma/Drizzle CLIs, pg_dump, and most ORMs.

# --- Docker (db/docker-compose.yml) — the default, so this whole block is optional ---
# PGHOST=localhost
# PGPORT=5444
# PGDATABASE=docker
# PGUSER=docker
# PGPASSWORD=docker

# --- Hosted Postgres (e.g. Neon) ---
# Copy the connection string your provider gives you and split it into these fields.
# PGHOST=ep-example-pooler.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech
# PGDATABASE=neondb
# PGUSER=neondb_owner
# PGPASSWORD=npg_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# TLS. Required by most hosted providers; omit both for a local Docker database.
# PGSSLMODE=require
# PGCHANNELBINDING=require
